{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792369157,"nonce":"XPg/BCgDov3MUkeKSssZJygcz3U=","message":"Local clips are in ff83adca (local). GpuPrimitive gets local_clip_bounds and local_clip_radius (zero width is none; the struct is 32 vec4 now), and sdf_core with its vb and dt variants test the sample point, already taken back through any transform, against the rect in the primitive's own frame, with the clip corner shape the screen clip uses. A turned parent therefore clips its children to its turned rounded box rather than to a bounding box, and a rounded clip cut by a plain one is exact (the producer writes both a screen clip and a local one for it). Decoded for boxes and glyphs; an image under one is still Unsupported::LocalClip, since the image pipeline has no clip in the image's own frame, and a shadow has none. Checked on a real device against CPU oracles: a turned rounded card with an overflowing child at display scales 1 and 2, and a cut clip, worst error 1 of 255, and by mutation (disabling the clip fails by 204). Remaining: backdrop, canvases, clip-path frame, fade rect, notch, local clip on images.","files":null}]}